Subject: [PATCH] fonts: installed families scale per profile

With --fingerprint-noise, each installed font family is drawn and
measured 1 to 4 parts per thousand larger or smaller, by a factor fixed
per profile and family. Profiles on one computer otherwise measure text
identically: measureText, DOMRect, Range rects, offsetWidth, emoji boxes
and SVG getBBox all came out equal across profiles. The factor is
applied to the font size where the platform font is created, so shaping
advances, ink bounds, line metrics, layout, SVG and the glyphs a canvas
draws all change together and agree with each other, in pages and in
workers. Combining marks stay attached because the whole font scales.
Web fonts are not changed.

